  "status": "Refused",
  "actual_commencement_date": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed single-storey rear extension, by virtue of its inappropriate scale and positioning, would result in a increased sense of enclosure on the neighbouring residents at 37 Alderney Avenue, which would harm the neighbours' living conditions, contrary to the Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD, and Local Plan Policies CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture) and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations), and the principles of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed single-storey rear extension, by virtue of its size and scale, would fail to be proportionate, subordinate and subservient to the host building. Instead, it would create a bulky and incongruous addition that would negatively impact the character and appearance of the host property and the surrounding area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Local Plan Policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture) and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations); the Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD, and the principles of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 3 - The porch extension, by reason of its size, scale, and design, would be incompatible and disproportionate to the host property and the surrounding area, detracting from the overall character of the neighbourhood. This is contrary to Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD and Local Plan Policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture), and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations)."
  ],
